+# Privacy and third-party review
+
+Scope: the static Daily Grind application in this repository. Review date: 2026-10-19. This is an internal code review and automated audit, not an independent certification.
+
+## Data inventory and minimization
+
+- No registration, checkout, forms, analytics, advertising, cookies, browser storage, or user database is implemented. Existing account/order/rewards links do not implement those services.
+- HTTP requests necessarily reach the server with connection metadata. The app processes requests in memory, ignores query strings for routing, and does not log requests, IP addresses, headers, bodies, or identifiers. No personal-data retention or backup exists in the app.
+- Only GET and HEAD are accepted. Other methods receive 405. Request data is never reflected into responses. Only explicitly listed public routes can be read; repository files and directory listings are inaccessible.
+- Responses use `Cache-Control: no-store`. There are no credentials, tokens, or secrets in client assets.
+
+## Third-party inventory and findings
+
+| Component | Data exposure | Review and action |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Unsplash hero photo | Previously each visitor contacted images.unsplash.com | Downloaded existing photo to public/assets/coffee.jpg; no visitor request to Unsplash remains. Source: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085. Recheck licensing and provenance before replacing the image. |
+| statikk via pnpm dlx | Runtime package download and transitive dependency exposure | Removed. Start now uses Node built-ins only; no npm runtime or development dependencies. |
+| Node.js | Handles HTTP connections | Use a supported, patched Node 22+ release. Review runtime security updates separately from npm packages. |
+| Hosting / reverse proxy | May receive IP addresses, request URLs, headers, and connection logs | Provider and configuration are not supplied in this repository. Deployment review is outstanding; see below. |
+| Fonts, analytics, scripts, embeds | None | Local styles and image only. CSP denies scripts, connections, forms, and external content. |
+
+Run `npm test` or `npm run audit:privacy` after asset, dependency, route, or integration changes. The automated audit checks public files for external resource references, scripts, forms, inline styles, and storage APIs; checks dependency declarations; and exercises live HTTP privacy controls. These checks are guardrails, not a substitute for reviewing new data flows. There is no third-party audit service integration and no independent audit has been commissioned.
+
+## Security headers
+
+The Node server applies headers to successful responses and application errors:
+
+- CSP: deny by default; allow only same-origin images and styles; deny scripts, connections, forms, plugins, base URL changes, and framing.
+- Referrer-Policy: no-referrer; X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff; X-Frame-Options: DENY.
+- Permissions-Policy disables camera, microphone, geolocation, payments, USB, and browsing topics.
+- Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy and Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin.
+- HSTS: max-age=31536000 when NODE_ENV=production. It deliberately does not enroll subdomains or request preload, since their HTTPS readiness is unknown.
+
+Reference for the CSP configuration: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP
+
+## Deployment requirements and outstanding review
+
+Start locally with `npm start` (port 11222 by default, override with PORT). In production run `NODE_ENV=production npm start` behind an HTTPS terminator. The Node listener serves HTTP internally: restrict its network access to the trusted proxy and configure the edge to redirect public HTTP to HTTPS. HSTS requires HTTPS and does not secure a first HTTP visit on its own. Do not expose the internal listener directly to the internet.
+
+Before production, the site operator must identify the hosting provider, review its subprocessors, data locations, access controls, contracts, retention, and deletion process. Disable access logging where possible; otherwise minimize/redact URLs, IPs and headers, restrict access, and set a short documented retention period. Check proxy, CDN, load balancer, monitoring, and backup settings; the app cannot control those systems. Update the public privacy notice with confirmed hosting practices. Ensure the edge preserves the security headers and applies equivalent protections to its own errors and redirects.
+
+Re-review vendors and dependencies before each integration and periodically after deployment. Assign an operator and review cadence at deployment. Record purpose, minimum fields, lawful handling requirements, recipients, retention, deletion, security controls, and user choices before adding personal-data features. Update CSP narrowly and add meaningful tests for each new data flow. Do not add tracking preemptively or claim an independent audit without one.
